------{1}::VARIABLE::------
::Local/global scoped::
1) Implicit(Auto)
A)var:-oldest keyword(use latest)
       -Global/local Scope
       -not blocked Scope
        i)to declare variable in JS.
        ii)Declare inside but access outside.
        iii)multiple redeclare/update with same name or in same scoped.
        iv)initialization after access.
B)let:-updated version(ES6)
      -blocked Scope
      i)Declare variable using let.
      ii)Declare locally but access global.
      iii)no redeclare with same name in same scope but in diff scope you can redeclare same name
      iv)you can also update value without let keyword.
      v)initialization after access.(undefined)
C)const:-updated version
        -block scoped
        -constant variable through out code.
        i)redeclare in same scope.you can not update.
        ii)reassignment in diff scope.

------{2}::DATA TYPES::------
-stores diff types of values
1)primitive:-predefined
            -build in data type 
            (String,number,boolean,undefined,null)
2)non-primitive:-programmer can update
                i)Object:
                        obj name={key:"value1",key2:"value2",...,keyN:"valueN"}
                ii)Array:
                        -store multiple values
                        -index starts from 0
                        array name=["val1","val2","val3",...,"val"]

------{3}::CONDITION AND LOOP::------
1)Condition:i)if
            ii)else if
            iii)if else
            iv)switch
            v)ternary

2)loop:i)for
       ii)do while
       iii)while
       iv)for of :-(best for array,string)
       v)for in(with array) 
       vi)for in(with object)    

------{4}::ARRAY METHOD::------
1)push() :-insert element(emd of array)
2)po()   :-remove element(last element)
3)map()  :-
4)filter()
5)forEach():-specifically(UX/UI)
6)includes()
7)find()

------{5}::OPERATORS::------
1)pre-increment  :(++a,immediately)
                  -increse value by 1 before use
2)post-increment :(a++,after use)
                  -use current value then increment by 1
3)pre-decrement  :(--a,immediately)
                  -decrese value by 1 before use
4)post-decrement :(a--,after use)
                  -use current value then decrese by 1

------{6}::FUNCTIONS::------
syntax: function functionname(para1,para2,....,paraN){
                //code
        }
        -->case 1 to 6
        - click(on click event):funcall--> output
syntax: function name=(para1,para2,..,paraN)=>expression(fat arrow)
        -->case 1 to 4
                -->case 1 to 3

------{7}::TEMPLATE LITERALS::------

1)normal string
2)varible interpolation
3)using Expression 
4)multiline string
5)HTML content

------{8}::POPUP BOXES::------

1)alert box(ok button-->for for dismiss box)
        :-ok-->on click-->fun()call-->popup window-->windowuser-->dismiss alert box

2)confirm box(ok(true)+cancle(false))
        :-ok-->on click-->fun()call-->popup window-->windowuser(ok)/(cancle)-->want/does not want

3)promt box(ok(entered value)+cancle(null))
        :-ok-->on click-->fun()call-->enters values


-----------{9}EMAR REGEX---------------
/^\w+([.-]?\w+)*@\w+([.]?\w+)*(\.\w{2,3})+$/
eg.lju.test@yahoo.co.in
1)^             :starts with            :
2)\w+           :name(letters,name.-)   :abc,abc123
3)([.-]?\w+)    :optional . or -in name :abc.abc,abc-abc
4)@             :must have              :@
5)\w+           :domain name            :gmail,yahoo,gov
6)([.]?\w+)     :subdomain name         :mail.nic
7)(\.\w{2,3})   :domain extension       :.co.in,.com,.in
8)$             :ends with email        :



